WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.111
CHIATECH JOURNAL explanatory summary: Netlify or Render for an Open-Access Journal Portal? Evidence-Based Deployment Selection for the CHIATECH JOURNAL Architecture

00:00:10.111 --> 00:00:25.556
Article focus: Background: CHIATECH JOURNAL is implemented as a crawlable static publication portal with a same-origin serverless editorial relay, a private Google Apps Script service and a private Google Sheet.

00:00:25.556 --> 00:00:36.111
Research context: The repository is already strongly coupled to Netlify through Functions, redirects, headers, deployment previews and release controls.

00:00:36.111 --> 00:00:52.889
Study approach: Objective: This study compared Netlify and Render to determine the better production deployment platform for the journal's current architecture and to identify the conditions under which migration would become technically justified.

00:00:52.889 --> 00:01:02.556
Reported findings: Methods: A technical case-study and weighted multi-criteria decision analysis were conducted on 17 July 2026.

00:01:02.556 --> 00:01:14.444
Interpretation: Primary evidence comprised the journal production guide, repository map, launch checklist, Netlify configuration, redirect/header rules, ignore rules and service-worker controls.

00:01:14.444 --> 00:01:23.667
Publication record: e004 · Volume 1, Issue 1 · July 2026 Pioneer Issue. DOI pending registration.
